WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.717
This is a run of my video planning and storyboard Skill.

2
00:00:03.717 --> 00:00:12.508
With three methods, brand film, IP drama and science explainer, it turns one request into an outline, shot sketches and an overview board.

3
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.790
Codex calls the Skill, reads the run guide, and checks image credits.

4
00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.676
The brief goes in word for word.

5
00:00:22.676 --> 00:00:24.913
It's open, so the Skill asks first.

6
00:00:24.913 --> 00:00:26.256
Brand film is picked.

7
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.731
The idea must pass a specificity test:

8
00:00:30.731 --> 00:00:35.701
AI repairs an old photo, but the daughter keeps her father's gap-toothed smile.

9
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.414
A tone frame comes first, setting light, colour and cast.

10
00:00:40.414 --> 00:00:42.922
Shot sketches start only after approval.

11
00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:47.926
Every image is checked.

12
00:00:47.926 --> 00:00:53.427
In shot one the hand misses the gap, so only that shot is redone, and the old one is kept.

13
00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.789
Once the key shot passes, the rest generate in parallel.

14
00:00:59.789 --> 00:01:00.569
Sped up here.

15
00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:07.214
Codex's self-review flags four more shots.

16
00:01:07.214 --> 00:01:09.789
Each is redone, with the reason logged.

17
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.832
Validation passes, and the overview board is built:

18
00:01:15.832 --> 00:01:18.371
eight shots, thirty-two seconds, vertical.

19
00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:23.127
Task two, same brief.

20
00:01:23.127 --> 00:01:26.627
The Skill asks again, and this time it's an IP drama.

21
00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:35.552
Azhi, a virtual girl, has a pocket that's only a texture.

22
00:01:35.552 --> 00:01:38.134
Keys slip through, so she wants a real one.

23
00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.426
After the tone frame, the identity reference drew a real pocket.

24
00:01:44.426 --> 00:01:46.970
That contradicts the story, so it's redone.

25
00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.868
Key shot first, the rest in parallel.

26
00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:52.566
All ten images pass review.

27
00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:57.894
Validation passes:

28
00:01:57.894 --> 00:02:01.773
eight shots, forty seconds, characters and props consistent.

29
00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:07.588
Task three is a science explainer.

30
00:02:07.588 --> 00:02:11.503
The question is clear, so the Skill classifies it without asking.

31
00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:15.308
Facts first:

32
00:02:15.308 --> 00:02:19.020
this is enzymatic browning, and every claim gets a source.

33
00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.591
The tone frame uses real kitchen objects.

34
00:02:25.591 --> 00:02:26.530
Clarity first.

35
00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:34.243
The mechanism is labelled illustrative, not a micrograph.

36
00:02:34.243 --> 00:02:35.949
Lemon juice is the control.

37
00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:39.729
Validation passes:

38
00:02:39.729 --> 00:02:42.859
four shots, thirty-two seconds, facts verified.

39
00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:51.066
All thirty-three sketches were made with GPT Image 2.

40
00:02:51.066 --> 00:02:55.589
Each task delivered an outline, shot sketches and an overview board.
